Tark: protected content (Widevine) is opt-in (spec 5.1, 5.3).

The component updater's URL file is kept out of domain substitution
(utils/domain_substitution_skip.txt), so its host is update.googleapis.com
again; its fallback becomes HTTPS. In return the updater accepts exactly one
component, the Widevine CDM, wherever a registration comes from, and the
startup list registers only that, only while Local State pref
tark.widevine_enabled is on. A Privacy settings toggle sets the pref:
turning it on registers Widevine and checks for it at once; turning it off
unregisters it, which deletes the downloaded module.

